@startuml orchestrator_class
title plogic - Orchestrator stage

skinparam classAttributeIconSize 0
hide empty members

interface UI {
}

class GUI {
}

class Orchestrator {
  +{static} evaluate(source: str, simplify: bool): Result<List<Evaluation>, List<Error>>
  +{static} simplify(source: str): Result<List<Formula>, List<Error>>
  +{static} assess(source: str, simplify: bool, max_variables: int?): Result<List<Assessment>, List<Error>>
  +{static} report(error: Error): str
  -{static} propositions(source: str): List<str>
}

class Evaluation {
  +proposition: str
  +original: str
  +table: TruthTable
  +simplification: Simplification?
}

class Formula {
  +proposition: str
  +simplification: Simplification
}

class Assessment {
  +formula: str
  +variables: int
  +simplification: Simplification?
  +table: TruthTable?
}

class Token

class Scanner
class Parser
class ScanState
class ParseState
class Simplifier
class Simplification
class Step
class Interpreter
class TruthTable
class InfixPrinter
abstract class Expression
enum Error

note bottom of Orchestrator
  Stateless: pure composition of the pipeline
  scan -> parse -> per proposition (simplify ->
  choose expression -> optional interpret). Failure is
  always signalled by Result, with Err = List<Error>.

  Stage gates: a scan failure stops before parsing,
  a parse failure stops before simplification, and
  an EvalError stops the whole run.

  evaluate() tabulates the simplified expression by
  default, or the original with --no-simplificar, and
  returns one Evaluation per proposition (table plus the
  Simplification when it ran). simplify() stops after
  simplification and builds no tables, returning one
  Formula per proposition.

  Both carry the proposition's source line, split out
  of the source before the scanner consumes it: the
  non-blank lines, trimmed, pair one to one with the
  parsed expressions (ADR-053).

  assess() is the GUI's entry point: it always returns
  the formula, its variable count and the steps, but
  builds a table only when max_variables is Some and the
  count is below it. None skips the table entirely. The
  GUI passes Some(10) when its table is on, so only
  fewer than ten variables are tabulated (ADR-049).
  report() is a pure formatter. All entry points take
  their owned argument by value (ADR-044, ADR-046,
  ADR-047, ADR-048, ADR-049).
end note

UI --> Orchestrator
GUI --> Orchestrator

Orchestrator ..> Scanner : <<use>>
Orchestrator ..> Parser : <<use>>
Orchestrator ..> Simplifier : <<use>>
Orchestrator ..> Interpreter : <<use>>
Orchestrator ..> TruthTable : with_display
Orchestrator ..> Evaluation : <<create>>
Orchestrator ..> Formula : <<create>>
Orchestrator ..> Assessment : <<create>>
Orchestrator ..> InfixPrinter : <<use>>
Orchestrator ..> Expression : <<use>>
Orchestrator ..> Error : <<use>>

Evaluation --> TruthTable : table
Evaluation --> Simplification : simplification
Assessment --> TruthTable : table
Assessment --> Simplification : simplification

Scanner ..> ScanState
Parser ..> ParseState
ScanState --> Token
ParseState --> Token
Interpreter ..> TruthTable : <<create>>
UI ..> TruthTable : <<use>>
GUI ..> Assessment : <<use>>

@enduml
